# SPRINT 68 — Platform Communication, Parent Access & 2FA Report

## 1. Scope
- Messaging System
- Announcements Module
- Parent Access
- Two-Factor Authentication

No Sprint 69/70/71 features were touched.

## 2. Source of Truth
- docs/specifications/teacher_features.md
- docs/specifications/student_features.md
- docs/specifications/assistant_features.md
- docs/specifications/shared_workflows.md

Extracted rules applied:
- Messaging: Teacher ↔ his enrolled students only, 1-to-1 threads per teacher-student pair, read/unread state, notification on new message. Assistant & Parent have no messaging access.
- Announcements: Teacher creates/edits/deletes own announcements targeted to his groups only; published_at gate; visible on Student Dashboard for enrolled students of targeted groups; produces notifications for targeted students only.
- Parent Access: real Parent account (mobile + password) linked automatically to students whose `parent_mobile` matches; registration requires ≥1 linked student; strictly read-only (profile + child student data); separate `parent` guard.
- 2FA: Email OTP for teachers only. Enable/disable from teacher settings with current-password confirmation. OTP hashed in cache (10 min TTL), sent by email, never logged or shown in UI. Challenge screen between password and session.

## 3. Existing Functionality Preserved
- Teacher/Student/Assistant login flows unchanged (students skip 2FA entirely).
- Existing notification infrastructure (`NotificationHelper`, `notifications` table) reused — no new notification system.
- All prior sprint feature tests still pass except 4 pre-existing legacy failures (see §12).

## 4. Messaging
- Tables: `messages` (teacher_id, student_id, sender_type enum teacher|student, body, read_at).
- Routes: teacher.messages.index/show/store, student.messages.index/show/store.
- Authorization: teacher can only message/view students enrolled in his groups; student can only access threads with teachers he is enrolled under; guests redirected; assistant/parent blocked.
- Read/unread: opening a thread marks incoming messages read; unread counts shown in lists.
- Notification of type `message` created for the recipient on each new message.

## 5. Announcements
- Tables: `announcements` (teacher_id, title, body, published_at), pivot `announcement_targets` (announcement_id, group_id).
- Teacher CRUD limited to own announcements; targeting validated against owned groups only (validation error otherwise).
- Visibility: Student Dashboard shows published announcements of groups the student is enrolled in; non-targeted students never see them.
- Notifications type `announcement` created for all targeted students on create/edit retarget.

## 6. Parent Access
- Table `parents` (name, mobile unique, password hashed, status) + `parent` auth guard in config/auth.php.
- Register: mobile must match ≥1 student's `parent_mobile`; auto-links to all matching students.
- Login: dedicated `/parent/login` with mobile+password; wrong credentials rejected with error.
- Dashboard: list of children; per-child page shows profile, attendance summary, grades summary, upcoming lessons, recent resources, notifications — all read-only.
- Security: parent cannot view unrelated students (403), cannot reach teacher/assistant/admin areas (403/redirect). Only write route is logout.

## 7. Two-Factor Authentication
- Type: Email OTP (6 digits), teachers only.
- Enable/Disable: POST teacher.two-factor.enable|disable requiring `current_password`; toggle stored on users.two_factor_enabled (boolean cast).
- Login challenge: after correct password, if two_factor_enabled → OTP issued (hashed in cache 10 min), redirect to /two-factor/challenge; guest until verified.
- Correct OTP → full login + session regenerate. Wrong/expired OTP → error, session cleared, must re-login.
- No backup codes (not required by spec). Secrets hashed; nothing logged; OTP not exposed in UI.

## 8. Bugs Found & Fixed
| Bug | Root Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 500 on announcement create (pivot insert) | `Announcement::groups()` used default pivot key `study_group_id` while migration used `group_id` | Explicit keys in belongsToMany |
| 500 on parent register/login | Missing `use App\Http\Controllers\Controller` import in ParentAuthController | Added import |
| two_factor_enabled returned int 0/1 | Missing boolean cast on User model | Added cast |
| OTP test could not capture code | Mail::raw content not inspectable via MailFake | Refactored send to `TwoFactorCode` mailable with public `$code` |

## 9. Root Causes Summary
All four bugs were implementation-level mismatches between migration schema/model definitions and Laravel conventions; no architectural changes required.

